// S441 reproducer — item 12: reads inside an engine opener effect= block are invisible to the W-DEAD-FUNCTION
// and E-DG-002 walkers (the README flagship docs/readme-snippets/tasks-app.scrml shows the same thing: a false
// W-DEAD-FUNCTION on its loader and E-DG-002 on its user-id and task-list cells).
// Compiler SHA: cf62b4154 (origin/main at dispatch)
// Command: bun compiler/bin/scrml.js compile docs/changes/s441-audit-gap-filing/repro/engine-effect-reads-invisible-to-dg.scrml --output-dir <scratch>
// Expected: no W-DEAD-FUNCTION on the helper and no E-DG-002 on the seed cell — the effect uses both.
// Actual:   exit 0 with W-DEAD-FUNCTION ("has no callers … It will be tree-shaken from the output") on the helper
//           and E-DG-002 ("declared but never consumed") on the seed cell. Neither is true: client.js keeps the
//           helper and the effect IIFE calls it with the seed cell's value. (E-DG-002 on the list cell is
//           correct — it is only written.)
// NOTE: this header deliberately avoids spelling the helper's or the cells' names. A `//` comment that
//       mentions them SILENCES both warnings — the reference walkers read comment text (measured; see the gap).
<program>
type Phase:enum = { Loading, Ready }
<seed>: number = 3
<items> = []
function build(n) { return [n, n + 1] }
<engine for=Phase initial=.Loading effect=${
    @items = build(@seed)
}>
    <Loading rule=.Ready>Loading</>
    <Ready rule=.Loading>Ready</>
</>
</>
